{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792415757,"nonce":"/B7PPBFOzyLhBUyNUhthPLe9N1A=","message":"Image clipping is in 7fdb57bb834aa7673faa0a4f530cf82dce967347 (local, not pushed). GpuImageInstance::abi_clip.x addresses a five-row auxiliary header: local bounds and radii, fade bounds and distances, and corner exponent, local AA and optional shape pointer. The existing shape payload follows, with relative polygon point offsets. The image shader composes the shared shape and shaped-rectangle helpers, samples the image through its existing transform, and multiplies screen, local, fade and shape coverage. Local coverage uses the producer's identity fringe and the analytic inverse-affine half-pixel otherwise. Native instances and plain ABI images keep a zero pointer and their previous clip path; plain images allocate no auxiliary rows. The instance is 13 vec4, 208 bytes. GpuPrimitive stays at 34 vec4, 544 bytes.\n\nImageDraw owns the auxiliary rows. Record::image_with_aux accepts the full list for polygon points, and render_images_with_aux uploads each draw's rows before binding them, so consecutive images cannot reuse a previous image's clip. Layers move the screen clip and fading rectangle, and translate the inverse shape frame through each nested texture origin; the local clip stays in image coordinates. LocalClip, ClipFade and ClipCorner are no longer unsupported reasons. Invalid or truncated shape data remains ClipShape. No ABI schema, shared ClipPath enum or CSS keyword changed.\n\nTwelve new fixtures came from blinc_abi a92f5c0's encoder. GPU-free tests cover scaling, separate fade bounds, polygon payloads and truncation, and zero auxiliary pointers for plain images. Both composed image shaders pass Naga validation. Offscreen Apple M1 Pro, Metal: all 23 display-list tests and the polygon fill-rule test pass. The twelve image scenes cover general affine local clips, independently transformed image and inherited shape frames, intersected fades, ellipse/rounded-rectangle/polygon clips, equal-orientation rings under both fill rules, a real producer's bevel clip corners, filtered layers with positive texture origins, nested layers, and overlapping consecutive images. At display scales 1 and 2, worst channel error against an independent CPU image-sampling and clipping oracle is 1/255. Only the layered polygon cases exclude probes near a polygon edge, 4 of 96,000 pixels each at scale 2, using the existing 0.001 logical-pixel guard; all other cases skip none.\n\nThe forced vertex-buffer path passes all 23 display-list tests. The forced data-texture image path also passes all twelve image scenes within 1/255 on Metal. For that check both storage capability flags were temporarily disabled and BLINC_GPU_MAX_PRIMITIVES/BLINC_GPU_MAX_GLYPHS set to 1024 to keep forced fallback textures within the requested device limits. Every override was restored. This checks image auxiliary texture reads only; ce34b20 still tracks stale SDF primitive packing. Actual WebGL2, PowerVR/Adreno compilation and mobile pixels remain unverified.\n\nMutation: disabling the image's local clip fails by 255/255. Removing inverse-frame translation into a layer texture fails by 153/255. The initial layer fixture had bounds touching the target origin, so that mutation had no effect; the fixture now moves both layer bounds strictly inside the target, and catches it. Opacity-only wrappers were flattened by the encoder, so the layer fixtures use a real brightness filter as well as opacity. Restored GPU tests pass.\n\nGate: fmt, workspace clippy, 1,887 workspace nextest tests (49 skipped), docs with warnings denied, wasm, iOS and threaded layout/CN tests pass. The separate DSL run has 516 passed, 28 failed, 10 skipped, with exactly the same failing names as the untouched ff83adca baseline recorded under a33d2b9. No dependency or DSL sources changed. Next: backdrop records, scoped in their own issue. Canvases still require agreement on the consumer API before implementation.","files":null}]}